From 16dd4c95d2689223f7d422a85a0d4ef4d7781f9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 06:15:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sppc: implement the public SL* surface instead of leaving
 it stubbed.

Office's licensing path calls into sppc.dll early, and a Wine `@ stub`
entry does not return -- stub_entry_point raises EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB,
which unwinds out of Office's own handler and kills the process. So a
stub here is strictly worse than a wrong answer: the caller never gets
to run its fallback.

All 49 public SL* entries are now real functions, following two rules:

  - queries return SL_E_VALUE_NOT_FOUND / SL_E_RIGHT_NOT_GRANTED, so the
    caller takes its "not licensed / not present" branch, which is a
    branch Office is built to handle;
  - actions return S_OK, because there is nothing observable to read
    back afterwards.

Found by running Word: SLSetAuthenticationData got it past the error (6)
dialog, then it demanded SLConsumeRight, then SLUnloadApplicationPolicies.
Rather than chase them one at a time, the remaining 30 are done here.

The 18 private SLp* entries stay stubbed -- nothing has called them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/sppc/sppc.c    | 320 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/sppc/sppc.spec |  86 ++++++------
 2 files changed, 363 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/sppc/sppc.c b/dlls/sppc/sppc.c
